<title>PHILIPPINES: PLDT rises 5.43 pct, spurred by dividend news.</title>
<headline>PLDT rises 5.43 pct, spurred by dividend news.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-03-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Philippine Long Distance Telephone Co rose by 85 pesos, or 5.43 percent, to 1,650 pesos in early trade on Wednesday as investors were encouraged by news of the company's 100 percent stock dividend declaration, brokers said.</p>
<p>&quot;The issue rose because of the dividend news. I think it was the first time in the history of PLDT to grant a 100 percent stock dividend,&quot; said Jonas Ferrer, research director at Pryce Securities.</p>
